Rinnie (Corrinna Desert)
Age: 12 Mana: No glow. A cup.
Appearance
Palette: Black and white. Small, thin for age. Black hair, black eyes, pale skin, soft features. Persistent dark circles under eyes. Hair tied up with a frayed ribbon — gift from Dusty; never without it. Faint warmth returning beneath pallor [see Backstory].
Personality
Genuine sweetness rooted in choice, not naivety — Stumps-raised, chose kindness because it costs nothing and means something. Learned from watching Dusty be gentle while starving. Quirky: mind drifts in associative chains that look random externally; names plants, talks to them, finds strange connections, states them flat. Observant — notices specifics before meaning, holds contradictions without resolving them. Mind is the part of her that isn't tired, so it wanders quietly. Thoughts loop back later with slightly more weight. Sadness sits underneath, surfaces only at triggers — hands shaking, hearing Dusty coming and fixing her face.
Masks condition for Dusty — deflects to his life, perfects reassuring smile [see Body Language]. Knows he almost sees through it. Does it anyway: his worry costs more than her pretending.
Gratitude expressed through action: pressed flowers, remembering names from single mentions, asking specific questions visits later.
Plants — the one domain where she's protector instead of protected. Unguarded there: bossy, funny, herself.
The Ghost
Quiet certainty of being a burden. Carries it silently — telling him would only add weight.
Want
To not cost Dusty anything more. To convince him she's fine.
Need
To accept she is not a burden.
Flaws
Major: Compulsive masking — hides her true condition to protect others, costs honest connection, may prevent full treatment. Minor: Deflects all attention from herself; makes relationships one-directional. Minor: Passive acceptance of illness — stopped expecting recovery.
Fear
Major: Dusty's sacrifices breaking him — her fault. Minor: Having a bad day when Dusty visits. Minor: Unable to care for her plants.
Speech
Voice: Plain, short sentences — economical, not childish. Shaped by scarcity. Occasionally oddly precise from years of watching instead of doing. Questions are her main tool — specific, remembered, aimed outward to show care and deflect attention. Humor dry and small. Quirky observations delivered flat, no punchline, no bid for reaction. Unguarded only with plants: bossy, funny, a little weird.
Dialogue Samples:
Casual: "Clouds and bread dough look the same when they're not done yet."
Under pressure: "The healer says I need more sunlight. I told her I'm not a fern."
Emotionally open: "I count sometimes. The things you'd have if it wasn't for me."
Body Language: Movements small, contained — conserves energy by habit, not timidity. Hands drift to soil or plant leaves instinctively; grounding gesture. Sits straighter when Dusty visits — visible effort, drops when she forgets. Tucks trembling hands under blankets / behind back when shaking starts. Tilts head when listening; stillness reads as full attention, not fatigue. Fingers trace surfaces absently — table edges, pot rims, seams of her blanket.
Backstory
Parents died to disease. Raised in the Stumps (economical homeless zone) by Dusty, who provided food and shelter. Chronic undiagnosed illness: systemic weakness. Symptoms — fatigue, pallor, trembling on overexertion. Good days: tends plants a few hours before hands shake. Bad days: bedbound. Healer theories (mana deficiency, blood weakness, congenital) — none confirmed. Illness simply is; Rinnie stopped expecting it to have a name.
